{% tool-context
   title="Architecture Diagram Builder"
   question="What is an architecture diagram?"
   definition="An architecture diagram is a working model of component ownership, trust boundaries, request paths, and state. It should expose decisions clearly enough to test before implementation."
   inputs="Place components with distinct responsibilities, connect each synchronous, asynchronous, or data path, and record capacity, replicas, and boundary ownership."
   outcome="Produce a reviewable topology where every dependency has a purpose and critical paths have explicit capacity and redundancy."
   experiment="Use Challenge mode to raise traffic or fail a component, then resolve every overloaded, disconnected, unbounded, or single-replica critical node." /%}

